export const summary = "What we collect, why, who receives it, how long we keep it, and your choices.";
export const html = "<p>This policy explains how <strong>Availeron Consulting, Inc.</strong>, 745 5th Ave., Suite 500, New York, NY 10151, United States (\"we\", \"us\"), handles personal information on Overhype.me. Questions and requests: <a href=\"mailto:privacy@overhype.me\">privacy@overhype.me</a>.</p>\n<p>Overhype.me is offered only in the places listed in our <a href=\"/terms\">Terms</a> and only to adults. It is not offered in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom.</p>\n<h2>What we collect</h2>\n<p><strong>When you browse, signed in or not</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Technical information</strong>: your IP address, browser and device type, the pages you visit, and when. Our hosting and security providers process this to deliver and protect the site.</li>\n<li><strong>How you use the site, for fixing errors.</strong> Our error-monitoring provider records some visits, and every visit in which an error happens: what the page showed and how it was used, with anything you type into a field hidden but other text on the page, including names shown in facts, visible. It also receives error details and page-speed measurements.</li>\n<li><strong>Your approximate location</strong> (country), worked out from your IP address by our network provider. We use it to decide which marketing-email default to show you and, as described in our Terms, where the Service is offered.</li>\n<li><strong>Names you type to personalise facts</strong> are kept in your browser, and sent to our servers when they are needed to show or make something with them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>When you create an account</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your email address and password (stored only as a one-way hash), or, if you sign in with Google or Apple, the email address and name they share with us.</li>\n<li>Your date of birth, the name and pronouns you choose, and your marketing-email choice, with the date you made it and the wording you were shown.</li>\n<li>Your acceptance of these policies, when we start recording it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>When you use the Service</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Content you create</strong>: facts, comments, votes, reactions, the memes and pictures you make, and searches you run.</li>\n<li><strong>Photos you upload.</strong> A photo is a picture of your face. We use it only to make the pictures and memes you ask for, and to show it as your profile photo if you choose.</li>\n<li><strong>Payments</strong>: if you buy a membership, Stripe collects your card details directly; we receive your Stripe customer reference, what you bought and its status, never your full card number.</li>\n<li><strong>Messages you send us</strong>, and records of reports and safety reviews.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>How we use it</h2>\n<p>To run the Service and your account; to make the pictures you ask for; to moderate content and keep people safe; to process payments; to send you emails about your account and, if you agreed, our newsletter; to prevent abuse and fraud; to fix problems; and to meet our legal obligations, including reporting apparent child sexual abuse material to the National Center for Missing &#x26; Exploited Children.</p>\n<p><strong>We do not sell your personal information</strong>, and we do not share it for advertising targeted on other sites.</p>\n<p><strong>Photos.</strong> We check that a photo shows a face, but we do not build face templates from it, recognise you, or identify anyone. We do not use your photos to train artificial-intelligence models. fal.ai's terms say it will not use what we send it to train models, apart from models it marks as excluded; we are checking the models we use against that list and will update this policy with the result.</p>\n<h2>Who receives it</h2>\n<p>We share personal information only with the providers that run parts of the Service for us, and only what each needs:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Provider</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n<th>What it receives</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Replit (with Google Cloud)</td>\n<td>Hosts the site, database and stored files</td>\n<td>Everything the Service stores</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cloudflare</td>\n<td>Network, security, bot checks</td>\n<td>Your IP address and requests</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>fal.ai and the image models it runs</td>\n<td>Makes AI pictures</td>\n<td>Your photo and the prompt for that picture</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>OpenAI</td>\n<td>Writing aids and content checks</td>\n<td>Fact and comment text, and in some checks a photo</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Project Arachnid (Canadian Centre for Child Protection)</td>\n<td>Detects known child sexual abuse material</td>\n<td>Uploaded images</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Stripe</td>\n<td>Payments</td>\n<td>Your email, account reference and purchases</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Resend</td>\n<td>Sends email</td>\n<td>Your email address and the message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sentry</td>\n<td>Finds and diagnoses errors in the site</td>\n<td>Error details and page-speed measurements; recordings of some visits and of every visit with an error, showing the page's text but not what you type; for signed-in members, your account ID, email address and name; and anything you send through its feedback button</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Google Analytics</td>\n<td>Counts visits</td>\n<td>Your IP address, pages visited and device information, with a random identifier</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Google Fonts</td>\n<td>Serves a typeface</td>\n<td>Your IP address</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Google and Apple</td>\n<td>Sign-in, if you choose them</td>\n<td>What you approve in their sign-in screen</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>We also disclose information when the law requires it, to protect people from harm, in connection with a sale or reorganisation of the business, or with your permission.</p>\n<p><strong>Sharing by email.</strong> If you share something by email, we send it to the address you enter. We use that address only to send that one message and to limit abuse of the feature.</p>\n<h2>How long we keep it</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Information</th>\n<th>How long</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Your account</td>\n<td>Until you delete it. Deletion takes effect 14 days after you ask, so you can change your mind; an open payment dispute delays it until the dispute is settled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>An account that never finished signing up</td>\n<td>Once it is 30 days old it is scheduled for deletion and we email you; it is deleted 14 days later unless you choose to keep it. An account you choose to keep is then kept like any other</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Photos, memes and pictures you delete</td>\n<td>Removed 30 days after you delete them; a backup copy is kept 7 more days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Your photos, memes and pictures when your account is deleted</td>\n<td>Removed when the deletion takes effect, with the same 7-day backup</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Facts you submitted</td>\n<td>Kept in the catalogue after you leave, credited to \"a former member\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Comments, votes and reactions</td>\n<td>Kept without your name after you leave; deleted if we remove your account for abuse</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sign-in sessions</td>\n<td>Valid for 7 days; removed when your account is deleted</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Records of how each picture was made</td>\n<td>Kept indefinitely, including the account and email address that made it, so a picture can be traced if it is misused</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Copies held by fal.ai</td>\n<td>Request data for up to 90 days under fal.ai's default settings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Child-safety evidence and reports</td>\n<td>As long as the law requires, and longer if we must preserve it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Delete your account</strong> from your profile at any time.</li>\n<li><strong>Delete any photo, meme or picture</strong> from \"My content\".</li>\n<li><strong>Marketing emails</strong>: you choose at sign-up.</li>\n<li><strong>Ask us</strong> to tell you what we hold about you or to correct it: write to <a href=\"mailto:privacy@overhype.me\">privacy@overhype.me</a>. We will verify that the request comes from you and answer within the time the law of your state requires.</li>\n<li><strong>California residents</strong>: you have the rights above. We do not sell or share personal information as California law defines those terms. You will not be treated differently for asking about your information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Do Not Track.</strong> Browsers' \"Do Not Track\" signals are not a standard we can act on, so we do not respond to them.</p>\n<h2>Children</h2>\n<p>Overhype.me is for adults and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 13. If you believe a child has given us information, write to <a href=\"mailto:privacy@overhype.me\">privacy@overhype.me</a> and we will delete it.</p>\n<h2>Security</h2>\n<p>We protect information with encryption in transit, access controls and limited staff access, but no service is perfectly secure. If a breach affects you, we will tell you as the law requires.</p>\n<h2>Changes</h2>\n<p>We will post any change here with a new version at the top of the page, and ask you to acknowledge significant changes.</p>\n<h2>Contact</h2>\n<p>Availeron Consulting, Inc., 745 5th Ave., Suite 500, New York, NY 10151, United States. <a href=\"mailto:privacy@overhype.me\">privacy@overhype.me</a>.</p>";
